Description: Record your screen with GPU acceleration
 Recording your screen on Wayland is usually one of two things: a tool that
 re-encodes on the CPU and turns your laptop into a heater, or a command line
 with fifteen flags. Easy Screen Recorder is the missing layer: capture stays
 on the GPU and you start recording in two clicks.
 .
 It records any monitor, a region you drag, the focused window or a camera,
 with an audio-only mode to Opus or FLAC that does not turn on video capture
 at all. Pause and resume mid-recording, a global shortcut, multiple audio
 tracks, and it tells you what is missing before you press record.
 .
 Independent frontend for gpu-screen-recorder; not affiliated with it. It
 drives gpu-screen-recorder as a separate external process and does not
 include or distribute it, so that program has to be installed separately.
 Run "easy-screen-recorder-cli --check" to see what is present and what is
 missing.
